==============================================================================
4. Candidate Meta-Hypotheses
==============================================================================
HYP-A: H and min-FAS are not functionally equivalent, but they share a monotone
       low-frequency component. FAS is the order parameter; H is the entropy
       inside each order stratum.
HYP-B: The graph-side 'dark H' should not be acyclic orientations alone:
       that statistic overlaps heavily between Royle-even and dark classes.
       A better analog should include the sign representation, e.g. a signed
       acyclic-orientation count weighted by automorphism edge sign.
HYP-C: The blind triads involving dark/even graphs, Krawtchouk/band limits,
       and feedback arc distance suggest a missing theory of the cycle-space
       quotient where distance-to-transitive and sign representation are dual
       projections of the same GF(2) object.
